      "impact": "A 10x larger boost input capacitance changes the boost converter's startup and inrush behaviour and no longer matches the PDI reference values used to size the EPD power stage.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["L1"],
      "pins": ["L1.1", "L1.2"],
      "nets": ["boost switch node / charge-pump node"],
      "observed": "The EPD driver sheet contains two 10 uH inductors (L2 and L1) and only two SS2040FL diodes (U4, U5).",
      "expected": "The PDI reference EPD driving circuit implemented here uses one 10 uH boost inductor and three SS2040FL rectifiers (U1/U2/U3 in the spec). A third rectifier position appears to be occupied by an inductor instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "L1 10uH (EPD_Driver sheet, vertical, next to C6/U4)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U1/U2/U3 | SS2040FL Schottky diodes (SOD-123FL) | EPD charge-pump/multiplier rectifiers ... L1 | 10 uH inductor | EPD boost-converter inductor"}
      ],
      "impact": "If a diode position is populated with an inductor, the EPD charge-pump/boost cannot rectify and generate the panel's VGH/VGL rails, so the display would not operate.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The EPD driver sheet deviates from the PDI reference the spec says it implements: C1 is 10 uF/6.3 V instead of the specified 1 uF/6.3 V G1-group value, and the sheet carries two 10 uH inductors (L1, L2) with only two SS2040FL diodes instead of the reference's one inductor and three diodes."
}

